## Derived from obamify

The engine in this project is a derivative work of
[obamify](https://github.com/Spu7Nix/obamify), MIT licensed,
copyright (c) 2025 Spu7Nix. A copy of that license is kept at
`crates/lab-core/assets/OBAMIFY-LICENSE-MIT.txt`.

What is derived, specifically:

| lebronify | obamify | what was taken |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `crates/lab-core/src/cost.rs` | `src/app/calculate/mod.rs` (`heuristic`) | the cost formula, verbatim |
| `crates/lab-core/src/solvers.rs` | `src/app/calculate/mod.rs` (`process_genetic`), `src/app/calculate/drawing_process.rs` | solver structure, constants, stopping rule |
| `crates/lab-core/src/solvers.rs` (`solve_optimal`) | `src/app/calculate/mod.rs` (`process_optimal`) | Kuhn-Munkres, inlined the same way and for the same reason (progress and cancellation) |
| `crates/lab-core/src/settings.rs` | `src/app/calculate/util.rs` (`GenerationSettings`, `CropScale`), `src/app/gui.rs` | field semantics, defaults, slider ranges, the proximity calibration step |
| `crates/lab-core/assets/lebron-target-256.png` | `src/app/calculate/target256.png` | the target image, renamed |
| `crates/lab-core/assets/lebron-weights-256.png` | `src/app/calculate/weights256.png` | the importance mask, renamed |
| `crates/lab-core/src/target.rs` | `src/app/calculate/util.rs` (`get_images`, `load_weights`) | crop-then-resize order and the red-channel weight read |

The shaders and the fluid simulation in upstream obamify were read to fix the
engine's numbers but no code from those files has been copied yet. When the GPU
renderer and the simulation are ported they belong in this table too.

## What is new

Everything that makes this more than obamify is original to this project:

* the [`Medium`](crates/lab-core/src/medium.rs) contract and the reducers in
  `crates/lab-media`
* the [`Assignment`](crates/lab-core/src/lib.rs) and `Artifact` types, including
  validation and the on-disk format
* the CLI, the renderers in `crates/lab-export`, and the before/after strip
* the no-network guard in `xtask/src/guard.rs`
* the media matrix and the generated documentation

## Asset attribution

LeBron James's likeness is used for the same reason obamify uses it: as the
canonical joke target of the transformation. The target and mask images are
inherited from upstream and are not covered by this project's license grant
beyond what upstream's MIT license conveys.